---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="KickzBrary Accessibility"
  description="Accessibility information for KickzBrary by HSL Innovations."
>
  <section class="page-hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p>
    <div class="page-app-icon">
      <img
        src="/icons/kickzbrary.png"
        alt="KickzBrary app icon"
        class="app-icon"
      />
    </div>
    <h1>KickzBrary</h1>
    <p>
      KickzBrary is designed so collectors can catalog, browse, and explore
      their sneaker collections comfortably, with support for Apple
      accessibility features throughout the app.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card">
    <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
    <p>
      HSL Innovations believes accessibility is part of thoughtful design.
      KickzBrary is built with clear layouts, readable text, descriptive
      controls, and support for Apple accessibility features.
    </p>

    <h2>VoiceOver</h2>
    <p>
      KickzBrary includes VoiceOver support to help users navigate their
      collection and the app's features.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Buttons and controls use descriptive labels and hints.</li>
      <li>Related information is grouped so it is read together.</li>
      <li>Statistics and values are announced in a meaningful way.</li>
      <li>Decorative images are hidden from VoiceOver to reduce clutter.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Dynamic Type</h2>
    <p>
      KickzBrary uses Apple's Dynamic Type text styles, so text grows with the
      size set in iOS or iPadOS. At the largest accessibility text sizes, some
      screens, such as collection statistics, switch to layouts that give
      larger text more room.
    </p>

    <p>
      Where space is limited, KickzBrary supports the Large Content Viewer so
      controls can be read at a larger size by touching and holding them.
    </p>

    <h2>Appearance</h2>
    <p>
      KickzBrary supports Light and Dark appearance. You can follow your
      device's system setting or choose a preferred theme within the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Reduce Motion</h2>
    <p>
      When Reduce Motion is turned on in your device's accessibility settings,
      KickzBrary minimizes animations in areas such as onboarding, card
      previews, and progress overlays.
    </p>

    <h2>Device Support</h2>
    <p>
      KickzBrary is designed for iPhone and iPad, with layouts that adapt to
      different screen sizes.
    </p>

    <h2>Ongoing Improvements</h2>
    <p>
      Accessibility is an ongoing effort. Future updates may improve VoiceOver
      navigation, layout behavior, text scaling, contrast, and other parts of
      the experience based on testing and user feedback.
    </p>

    <h2>Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you encounter an accessibility issue or have suggestions for improving
      KickzBrary, please contact HSL Innovations through the <a href="/support/kickzbrary">KickzBrary Support page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
